<p>The Trump administration says it has begun pulling about 1,000 U.S. troops out of Syria. Multiple outlets describe the move as a drawdown, though the Wall Street Journal, citing U.S. officials, said it could widen into a full withdrawal of the remaining American force. Officials and news reports place the shift alongside Syria’s new government as it works to consolidate control, while the threat from ISIS remains a central concern.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Conditions-based framing: A senior U.S. official called the troop departures a “deliberate and conditions-based transition,” not a fixed-date pullout.</li><li>Verification note: Reuters said it could not immediately verify the Wall Street Journal report that the U.S. is withdrawing all remaining troops.</li><li>Base handover (last week): Reuters reported that the U.S. military finished leaving a strategic base in Syria and handed it to Syrian forces, describing it as a sign of strengthening U.S.-Syrian ties that could open the door to a larger drawdown.</li><li>Regional backdrop: PBS linked the timing to broader regional tensions, saying Iran appeared to be bracing for a possible U.S. strike as tensions rose.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration official (via PBS): A senior administration official told PBS News the U.S. will reduce the number of troops fighting ISIS in Syria, framing it as part of a changed U.S. approach. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/u-s-cuts-forces-in-syria-as-its-new-government-fights-terror-threat'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Wall Street Journal (citing U.S. officials): The Wall Street Journal reported, citing three U.S. officials, that the U.S. is withdrawing all remaining troops from Syria and formally ending its military presence there. (<a href='https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/syria-us-troops-withdraw-a97a2665'>The Wall Street Journal</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera (on expected pace): Al Jazeera reported that U.S. officials expect the withdrawal from remaining positions to finish within two months. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/18/us-is-withdrawing-all-1000-troops-from-syria-wsj-report'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1r8mb6d/us_to_withdraw_troops_from_syria_amid_iran/'>US to withdraw troops from Syria amid Iran tensions</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/u-s-cuts-forces-in-syria-as-its-new-government-fights-terror-threat'>U.S. cuts forces in Syria as its new government fights terror threat</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-pulls-forces-from-syria-as-new-government-exerts-control'>US pulls forces from Syria as new government exerts control</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/us-withdrawing-all-forces-syria-wsj-reports'>US withdrawing all forces from Syria, WSJ reports</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/18/us-is-withdrawing-all-1000-troops-from-syria-wsj-report'>US is withdrawing all 1,000 troops from Syria: WSJ report</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/syria-us-troops-withdraw-a97a2665'>The United States announces that it will withdraw all remaining military troops from Syria, formally ending its 12-year military presence in the country.</a> - wsj.com</li></ul>